        "category": "engine",
        "title": "P0303 — Cylinder 3 Misfire from Ignition Coil/Plug or Intake-Valve Carbon Buildup on the 1.5L Turbo",
        "description": "P0303 (cylinder 3 misfire) shows up frequently on the 2016-2018 Malibu 1.5L turbo (LFV) and is discussed heavily on the Malibu forums. The direct-injected 1.5T is prone to carbon buildup on the intake valves, which disrupts airflow and causes lean/rough combustion and misfires; a GM service bulletin describes misfire conditions from significant carbon buildup due to incomplete fuel burn. On top of that, a weak coil or worn spark plug at cylinder 3 is the classic ignition-side cause. Fuel injector #3 problems and PCV/vacuum leaks can contribute. Because the difference between a plug and a valve-carbon repair is large, proper diagnosis matters.",
        "solution": "Inspect and, if worn/fouled, replace the cylinder 3 spark plug; swap the #3 coil with an adjacent one to see if the misfire follows it and replace the coil if so. If ignition parts are good and misfire persists, check for carbon buildup on the intake valves (per GM bulletin) and perform a walnut-blast/intake-valve cleaning; verify injector #3 and check for vacuum/PCV leaks. Stop driving if the CEL flashes to protect the catalytic converter.",
